# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-plugin-loader — discover and load plug-ins (source and compiled), install layout
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: feature
#+DEPENDS: alfe-plugin-spec-and-manual
#+BRANCH: master

* Context

Sub-issue of =alfe-plugin-model=. Layout decided by pjb (2026-09-21):
=${PREFIX}/share/clautolisp/plug-in/${name}/${name}.lisp= (source) or
=${name}.${alfe-version}-${impl}.plugin= (compiled), or the equivalent under
the user's XDG data directory. Plug-ins are Common Lisp.

* Proposal

- New file =source/plugin.lisp= (package =alfe.plugin=, in
  =autolisp-front-end/core=, before =cli=).
- *Search path*, first plug-in of a given name wins (so a local install
  shadows a system one): =--plugin-path DIR= (repeatable), =$ALFE_PLUGIN_PATH=
  (a PATH-style list), =$XDG_DATA_HOME/clautolisp/plug-in= (default
  =~/.local/share=), each =$XDG_DATA_DIRS= entry + =/clautolisp/plug-in=
  (default =/usr/local/share:/usr/share=), =<PREFIX>/share/clautolisp/plug-in=
  from the running executable (=installation-prefixes=).
- *Forms.* Compiled file =NAME.<alfe-version>-<impl>.plugin= where impl is
  =sbcl= / =ccl=; loaded when it exists and is at least as new as the
  source; otherwise the source is loaded. A compiled file for another
  version or implementation is ignored (logged at -v). A compiled file that
  fails to load falls back to the source with a warning.
- *Compiling.* =alfe --compile-plugin FILE.lisp= writes the compiled form
  next to the source, for the running alfe version and implementation, and
  exits. =make install= installs the shipped plug-ins and compiles them with
  the just-built alfe.
- *Failure isolation.* A plug-in that fails to load (read error, compile
  error, =register-plugin= error) is reported on stderr as a warning and
  skipped; alfe carries on.
- Options: =--plugin-path DIR=, =--no-plugins= (=$ALFE_NO_PLUGINS=),
  =--list-plugins= (name, version, form loaded, path, description),
  =--compile-plugin FILE=. =--plugin-path= and =--no-plugins= are found by a
  pre-scan of argv because they decide what is loaded *before* the parser
  learns the plug-in options; the parser still accepts them.

* Acceptance criteria

- A source plug-in and a compiled plug-in each load, under SBCL and CCL
  (the compiled file has a =.plugin= type, which CCL's =load= must accept).
- Shadowing order, wrong-version and wrong-implementation compiled files,
  a broken plug-in (alfe still runs), =--no-plugins=, =--list-plugins=,
  =--compile-plugin= are covered by unit tests and scenarios.
- =make install= puts plug-ins under =$(PREFIX)/share/clautolisp/plug-in/=.

* Resolved (alfe 2.2.76)

=source/plugin.lisp= part 5 and =alfe.cli:run=. Search path as specified plus
a sixth root, the source tree's =plugins/= (last; what makes the shipped
plug-ins work from a checkout, as =:vendored= does for the CAD runtime files).
A process-wide cache of loaded files (path + write date) keeps the test suite,
which calls =run= hundreds of times, from recompiling a plug-in per call; it
is never read by a process that runs alfe once.

Verified: 110 plug-in / CLI / conformance tests under SBCL and CCL (the
compiled =.plugin= loads under both); a built =alfe-sbcl= installed with
=make install-programs install-plugins= into a scratch prefix loads the
compiled forms in preference to the source tree's. The full CCL suite could
not be run to the end: see =ccl-protocol-write-atomic-file-contention-hangs=.
